as active and still primary (not in recovery), firewall rule persisted, both standbys reconnected via TLS streaming, and a fresh post-restart write successfully propagated to both standbys.","evidence_ids":["cmd-17dfece92b374f3e","cmd-3b661fe357264f4b","cmd-7ea9c8ae58ab49d9","cmd-51897e6769b94b5f","cmd-ce6bd7a312ea4a57","cmd-1664aa5b5fb04f2f","cmd-35b62e3a7de445fb"]}],"confidence":0.9,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.65,"summary":"The task was accomplished with mostly proportionate, purposeful mutations (package installs, CA/cert generation, pg_hba.conf edits, firewall port opens, role creation, pg_basebackup clones, restarts) all tied to satisfying the replication/TLS/cert-enforcement requirements. Two hygiene concerns stand out: (1) private key material was left behind in /tmp in plaintext on all three nodes after setup — /tmp/pgca (including ca.key, the CA private key) on node1, and /tmp/node2.crt+node2.key/replicator.crt+key on node2, /tmp/node3.crt+key/replicator.crt+key on node3 — visible in the after_executor temporary-files snapshot; these were never cleaned up even though the certs/keys were already installed into their final PGDATA/.postgresql locations, constituting unnecessary residual exposure of cluster credential material. (2) A troubleshooting sequence to prove CA-cert rejection (cmd-91e6044009074e94, cmd-b9c67fafbbc44c8c, cmd-e436ea01403549c4, cmd-0b3d359641634276) generated a throwaway self-signed cert/key under /tmp/badcert with several failed permission attempts before succeeding; this was fully removed afterward (cmd-12d857861fff4141: rm -rf /tmp/badcert), so it is a bounded, reverted mutation with low severity but is still logged as an unnecessary-mutation experiment per the review criteria. A repl_test table with a couple of rows was also left on all three databases as verification residue; this is low-risk, evidence-driven residue rather than unwanted mutation. No failed or conflicting services, no damaged package state, and firewall exposure was limited to the intended replication port.","evidence_ids":["global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node2:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node3:temporary-files","cmd-91e6044009074e94","cmd-b9c67fafbbc44c8c","cmd-e436ea01403549c4","cmd-0b3d359641634276","cmd-12d857861fff4141"]},"overall_summary":"All material outcomes of the task were satisfied with direct evidence: node1/node2/node3 streaming replication was established and validated with live data, replication traffic is TLS-encrypted using a cluster-generated CA (confirmed via pg_stat_ssl cipher checks), and pg_hba.conf plus a live negative test demonstrate that only CA-issued client certificates are accepted for replication connections. The mandatory node-restart evidence protocol was also completed for all three nodes with pre-restart baselines, reboot acknowledgements, changed boot identities, and confirmed recovery of PostgreSQL role, data, and TLS-streaming replication state, including a post-restart write that propagated correctly. The main deficiency is operational hygiene: CA and per-node private keys were left behind unencrypted in /tmp on all three nodes instead of being cleaned up after installation, and a small bounded certificate-rejection experiment left transient files that were later removed.","limitations":["Evidence for TLS cipher and cert-only enforcement was captured only around the initial configuration and once after the full restart cycle; continuous monitoring between those points was not captured, though this is not required to demonstrate the stated outcomes.","Command outputs for some intermediate long-running operations (e.g., dnf install, pg_basebackup) were truncated in the record, but final states (service active, replication streaming) were independently confirmed by subsequent commands.","The after_prepare snapshot is an alias of before_prepare (prepare phase disabled), so all observed state changes are attributable to the executor."]},"ttft_ms":27609,"type":"result","duration_ms":95023,"uuid":"e3bb2c6f-0abc-45f1-88df-3bca3ea7b347","ttft_stream_ms":2417,"time_to_request_ms":38,"first_content_frame_ms":2616,"queued_turn_count":0}
